BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wake-no-phone-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T080500
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Wake up - no phone rule
DESCRIPTION:Cortisol awakening response window. Lie still and breathe for 5 minutes. No phone - checking notifications floods the CAR with stress hormones and dysregulates your whole morning.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Wake up - no phone for first 5 minutes
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dog-walk-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T080500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T081500
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Dog walk - light exposure (10 min)
DESCRIPTION:Outdoor light exposure block. 2500+ lux suppresses residual melatonin and enhances cortisol awakening response by 20-40%. Let the dog set the pace. No phone scrolling.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Dog walk - get outside for light exposure
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:breakfast-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T082000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T084500
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Hydration + Breakfast (25 min)
DESCRIPTION:Start with 500ml water. Then eat - ghrelin peaks in the morning. Protein provides tyrosine for dopamine synthesis. High fiber and fat keeps you full through the commute walk. Target: ~350-420 kcal with 18-28g protein.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Drink 500ml water then eat your prepared breakfast
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meditation-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T084500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T090000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Meditation (10-15 min)
DESCRIPTION:Optimal window for your late chronotype. Cortisol has peaked and is beginning its gentle decline. Brain is alert but not yet task-loaded. A single 13-minute session measurably improves attention and working memory hours later. Use breath focus or a body scan. Silence or ambient sound only.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Meditation - 10 to 15 min breath focus before shower
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shower-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T091000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Cold water + Shower (10 min)
DESCRIPTION:End shower with 30-90 seconds of cold water. Triggers norepinephrine release up to 300%, dopamine, and serotonin. Increases neural connectivity in the prefrontal cortex and anterior cingulate - your decision-making centers.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Shower - end with 30 to 90 sec cold water
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:commute-walk-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T094500
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:Walk to office - planning walk (30 min)
DESCRIPTION:BDNF-boosting movement plus default mode network priming. No podcasts for first 15 min - let your mind surface ideas. Mentally rehearse your top 1-2 tasks. Arrive pre-loaded.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Leave for office - no headphones first 15 minutes
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:caffeine-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T095000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T095500
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:Caffeine - strategic timing
DESCRIPTION:110 minutes after waking. Adenosine has cleared sufficiently - caffeine amplifies alertness cleanly without the afternoon crash. Maximum 1-2 cups. No caffeine after 2 PM.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Caffeine window - adenosine sufficiently cleared now
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:planning-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T101500
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:Daily planning block (15 min)
DESCRIPTION:Write your 1-3 most important tasks. No email or Slack. You already rehearsed on the walk - this is just formalizing it. Externalizing priorities now means your peak window is pure execution.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Plan top 1-3 tasks - no email until this is done
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warmup-work-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T101500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T110000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:Warm-up work - low friction (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Code reviews, reading docs, async replies, writing tests. The synchrony effect shows late chronotypes perform worst on demanding tasks in the early morning. Save your peak for 11 AM.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Warm-up work - low friction tasks only, protect peak
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:deep-work-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T130000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:DEEP WORK - Peak window (2 hours)
DESCRIPTION:YOUR COGNITIVE PEAK. Architecture decisions, complex debugging, system design - anything requiring working memory and executive function. Calendar blocked. Notifications silenced. 90-min ultradian cycle. Research confirms late chronotypes have superior processing speed in this window.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:PEAK WINDOW - Block everything. Deep work only.
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lunch-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T133000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:Lunch (30 min)
DESCRIPTION:Her target: ~330-400 kcal with 16-38g protein. Use your prep-ahead options from the Hub. Avoid high-carb lunches that spike blood sugar and impair afternoon focus.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Lunch - grab your prepped meal
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:workout-weekday-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T174500
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
SUMMARY:Workout - Home or Pilates (4:30 PM)
DESCRIPTION:Physical performance peak for late chronotypes. Check your 3-week rotating plan in the Hub. Week 1 Menstrual: Pilates plus gentle activation. Week 2 Follicular: Solin glute build - heaviest week. Week 3 Luteal: Moderate load, high rep, glute shred. Dumbbells: 3 lb, 5 lb, 10 lb.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:15 min until workout - change and get ready
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Workout time - check your phase plan in the Hub
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:workout-weekend-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T110000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=SA,SU
SUMMARY:Weekend Pilates or Active Recovery
DESCRIPTION:Preferred Pilates day - reformer or mat class. If no class: use the home alternative from your Hub plan. Also a great time to prep 3 overnight oat jars for Mon-Wed, cook batch quinoa, make a jar of curtido, or start fermented jamaica.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Weekend Pilates or active movement
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dinner-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T193000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Dinner
DESCRIPTION:Her target: ~380-450 kcal with 38-52g protein. Close eating window by 8 PM for optimal overnight fasting. Check Hub recipes for ideas. Weeknight: 25-35 min prep. Weekend: more time to try new recipes.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Dinner time - check Hub recipes
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:breakfast-prep-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T204500
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Prep tomorrow's breakfast (5 min)
DESCRIPTION:Set out ingredients or make overnight oats. Takes 5 minutes but eliminates morning decisions during the cortisol awakening response window. Sunday night: make 3 jars for Mon-Wed at once.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Prep tomorrow's breakfast now
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wind-down-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250526T220000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
SUMMARY:Wind down - reduce screens
DESCRIPTION:Begin wind-down for your late chronotype. Dim lights, reduce blue light. Especially important during Week 3 luteal phase when progesterone disrupts sleep. Options: reading, gentle stretching, journaling, herbal tea. Target sleep: 11:30 PM to 7:30 AM minimum.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Wind down - dim lights and reduce screens
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sunday-prep-001@wellnesshub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250601T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250601T113000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=SU
SUMMARY:Sunday meal prep (30 min)
DESCRIPTION:Make 3 overnight oat jars for Mon-Wed breakfasts. Cook double batch quinoa for Wed-Fri lunches. Check grocery list in Hub. Marinate chicken if needed for Monday. Start curtido jar if running low. 20 minutes of prep sets up the whole week.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Sunday meal prep - 30 min to set up the whole week
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
